2) Results of Lab 1
Rule: My dice is unfair if the mean falls outside 2 standard deviations from the mean of a 'fair dice' 
Used R to simulate 100 experiments to act as a 'fair dice'. Each simulation had 20 rolls. 
Used R to calculate the mean roll value for each simulation. 
The average of the simulated means was 3.49. The standard deviation of the simulated means was 0.37. 
Two standard deviations of the simulation (2 s.d.s = 0.74) was between 2.75 and 4.23 was within 95% CI. 
My observed dice-rolling mean was 4.7 and 3.5. One dice fell outside the 95% CI. 
Result: One dice has evidence that is is 'unfair'.

3) Created Sportify playlist of 30 songs. I included 10 songs I most recently listened to. 10 songs I have listened to in the past. and 
10 songs I have never listened to by artists I do not know. 
Hypothesis- The first few songs will always be the songs I listened to the most. 
Testing- Simulated 10 times. Shuffled throughout the entire playlist (30 shuffles).
Tests 1-3 - first song in shuffle was usually one I played often. 
Tests 4-10 Middle shuffles seemed to be more random. At times 4 songs in a row would play that I had never played before.
The more I shuffled, the more it seemed like there was an equal probability of a song I knew, song I didn't know, 
and song I have listened to previously to come up in that order.
